explanation:
The body applies the library's `ClosedSubgroupScheme.mk` to the morphism `kostantRootSubgroupToToral`, the root-subgroup map factored through the toral carrier. The instance it needs, that this map is a closed immersion, is supplied by `isClosedImmersion_kostantRootSubgroupToToral`. That theorem is proved from the root-step hypotheses (`hc`, `hstep`, `hsq`), which make the coordinate map surjective. So the result is exactly the closed subgroup scheme given by the image of 𝔾ₐ under the root-subgroup morphism, which is what the docstring describes.

This is a specific object inside the Kostant/Chevalley construction. The special setting is part of the construction itself:
- a ℚ-Lie algebra L;
- a representation ρ of its enveloping algebra;
- a ℤ-lattice M with a finite basis, stable under the Kostant ℤ-form;
- nilpotent root operators.

Mathlib has no counterpart, since it has no Chevalley group schemes or Kostant root subgroups. The extra hypotheses only serve to discharge the closed-immersion instance, so they do not distort the object. The definition is not too narrow, because its content needs this setting.
